1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,936
**(Pre-Chorus - The Roast)**

2
00:00:08,936 --> 00:00:14,043
Alright fifth-semester, phones away, eyes on the board!

3
00:00:14,043 --> 00:00:19,388
Half of you failed the midterm because you do not know the difference between a pin and a roller.

4
00:00:19,388 --> 00:00:23,697
Today we are doing a lateral stability check on a steel beam.

5
00:00:23,697 --> 00:00:29,282
If you mess this up in the real world, the roof caves in.

6
00:00:29,282 --> 00:00:39,282
So pay attention. Hit the track!

7
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,723
Check the problem on the screen, read it and weep,

8
00:00:43,723 --> 00:00:45,957
I S M B three hundred, do not go to sleep!

9
00:00:45,957 --> 00:00:49,229
It is a simply supported beam with a span of five meters,

10
00:00:49,229 --> 00:00:51,862
Dealing with a factored load, pay attention you cheaters!

11
00:00:51,862 --> 00:00:54,096
Forty kilo-newtons per meter pushing it down,

12
00:00:54,096 --> 00:00:56,888
F E four ten grade steel, the strongest in town.

13
00:00:56,888 --> 00:00:59,761
Step one, calculate the moment, W L squared over eight!

14
00:00:59,761 --> 00:01:02,234
Forty times twenty-five over eight, do not hesitate!

15
00:01:02,234 --> 00:01:05,186
One hundred twenty-five kilo-newton meters is the demand.

16
00:01:05,186 --> 00:01:07,899
Now calculate the shear force, or get out of my class, understand?!

17
00:01:07,899 --> 00:01:10,931
W L over two! That is exactly one hundred kilo-newtons!

18
00:01:10,931 --> 00:01:13,324
Even a first-year student could reach these conclusions!

19
00:01:13,324 --> 00:01:13,644
**(Pre-Chorus - The Roast)**

20
00:01:13,644 --> 00:01:16,277
Are you writing this down? Or staring into space?

21
00:01:16,277 --> 00:01:19,548
Because when the building inspector comes, it is me they chase!

22
00:01:19,548 --> 00:01:23,936
Read the boundary conditions, open your eyes!

23
00:01:23,936 --> 00:01:28,723
The compression flange is laterally restrained throughout the length!

24
00:01:28,723 --> 00:01:33,989
That means no lateral torsional buckling to ruin our strength!

25
00:01:33,989 --> 00:01:37,340
The beam is fully supported, it is not twisting away!

26
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,973
We bypass the buckling equations and save the day!

27
00:01:39,973 --> 00:01:42,606
We are designing for pure yielding, keeping the structure intact,

28
00:01:42,606 --> 00:01:45,239
Laterally restrained from end to end, and that is a fact!

29
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:48,271
Now open your I S eight hundred, page eighteen, let us go!

30
00:01:48,271 --> 00:01:50,824
We classify the section so the capacity can flow.

31
00:01:50,824 --> 00:01:53,378
Flange width outstand, B over thickness T F,

32
00:01:53,378 --> 00:01:56,090
Seventy over twelve point four, are you suddenly deaf?!

33
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:58,963
It is five point six four! Less than nine point four epsilon!

34
00:01:58,963 --> 00:02:01,676
The flange is class one plastic, come on people, let us move on!

35
00:02:01,676 --> 00:02:04,149
Check the web depth D over thickness T W,

36
00:02:04,149 --> 00:02:06,862
Thirty-two point nine, well under eighty-four, I am telling you!

37
00:02:06,862 --> 00:02:09,495
The whole section is plastic! Beta B equals one!

38
00:02:09,495 --> 00:02:14,202
This beam will form a plastic hinge before the failure has begun!

39
00:02:14,202 --> 00:02:16,676
Let me slow it down for a second.

40
00:02:16,676 --> 00:02:19,309
Breathe.

41
00:02:19,309 --> 00:02:22,660
Why do we check the design shear capacity? V D?

42
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:25,133
Because if the web shears... the whole system collapses.

43
00:02:25,133 --> 00:02:30,399
Area of the web times the yield stress... divided by root three and gamma M zero.

44
00:02:30,399 --> 00:02:33,431
That is two hundred ninety-five kilo-newtons.

45
00:02:33,431 --> 00:02:35,984
Our applied shear is only one hundred.

46
00:02:35,984 --> 00:02:40,851
We are below sixty percent. We are in a low shear condition.

47
00:02:40,851 --> 00:02:43,245
Do you know what that means?

48
00:02:43,245 --> 00:02:45,718
It means no reduction!

49
00:02:45,718 --> 00:02:49,229
It means we get to use the full bending strength!

50
00:02:49,229 --> 00:02:51,223
Brace yourselves!

51
00:02:51,223 --> 00:02:53,777
Bring in the plastic modulus, Z P on the track!

52
00:02:53,777 --> 00:02:56,330
Six hundred fifty-one point seven times ten cubed, do not hold back!

53
00:02:56,330 --> 00:02:59,043
Multiply by two hundred fifty, divide by one point one zero!

54
00:02:59,043 --> 00:03:01,995
One hundred forty-eight point one kilo-newton meters, you are the hero!

55
00:03:01,995 --> 00:03:04,468
Demand is one twenty-five! Capacity is one forty-eight!

56
00:03:04,468 --> 00:03:06,622
The section is adequate! The numbers are great!

57
00:03:06,622 --> 00:03:09,335
Check the elastic limit, one point two Z E F Y,

58
00:03:09,335 --> 00:03:14,202
One hundred fifty-six, we are perfectly safe, do not cry!

59
00:03:14,202 --> 00:03:19,388
I S M B three hundred passes the lateral stability check.

60
00:03:19,388 --> 00:03:23,218
It is safe. It is secure.

61
00:03:23,218 --> 00:03:28,644
And if you did not understand this... switch your major to business.

62
00:03:28,644 --> 00:03:33,681
Class dismissed.

